.TH NN-COMPARE 1 "2026" "nn 0.1.0" "NN Manual"
.SH NAME
nn-compare \- compare two models or backends on inputs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nn compare [options] <a> <b>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Without --input, compare structure. With inputs, run both models (each bound independently so ONNX vs TFLite names may differ) and compare outputs by name, then by index. Rank-4 NCHW/NHWC pairs are permuted when shapes match that layout. --activations compares intermediates when a backend can dump them (reference); ORT and LiteRT typically cannot dump all activations.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-input NAME=FILE
Input tensor (npy/npz/csv/raw); repeatable.
.TP
.B \-\-backend NAME
Backend for the first model.
.TP
.B \-\-backend2 NAME
Backend for the second model.
.TP
.B \-\-activations
Compare intermediate activations when available.
.TP
.B \-\-threshold VALUE
Divergence threshold on max abs (default 1e-5).
.TP
.B \-\-atol VALUE
Absolute tolerance.
.TP
.B \-\-rtol VALUE
Relative tolerance.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 similar; 1 different.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
nn compare float.onnx quant.tflite --input test.npy
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
nn-diff(1), nn-run(1)
